<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="ggrid" data-stagger><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/kansas-hail-claim-roof-schedules/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/hail-roof.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hail-roof-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hail-roof.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><small>Nov 3, 2026 · 7 min read</small><h2><a href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/kansas-hail-claim-roof-schedules/">Kansas Hail Claims, Roof Schedules and Cosmetic Exclusions</a></h2><p>Three policy features now decide many Kansas hail payouts. Here is how each works and how appraisal fits around them.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/appraisal-attorneys-and-kansas-fee-statutes/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="734" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><small>Oct 27, 2026 · 6 min read</small><h2><a href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/appraisal-attorneys-and-kansas-fee-statutes/">Appraisal, Attorneys and Kansas Fee Statutes: A Plain Overview</a></h2><p>Appraisal handles the amount of loss. Some disputes need a lawyer. Here is a careful, general look at the line between them in Kansas.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/documenting-tornado-damage-kansas/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><small>Oct 14, 2026 · 7 min read</small><h2><a href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/documenting-tornado-damage-kansas/">After a Kansas Tornado: Documenting Partial and Total Losses</a></h2><p>What to photograph, measure and save after a tornado or derecho so the amount of loss can be valued fully.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/grass-fire-claims-kansas-farms/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/grass-fire.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/grass-fire-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/grass-fire.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="1024" height="626" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><small>Sep 30, 2026 · 6 min read</small><h2><a href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/grass-fire-claims-kansas-farms/">Grass Fire Claims on Kansas Farms, Ranches and Acreages</a></h2><p>Prairie fires burn more than homes. Here is how fence, outbuildings and smoke damage are handled, and where disputes arise.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/choosing-an-appraisal-umpire/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/documents.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/documents-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/documents.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 33vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="gcard-b"><small>Sep 16, 2026 · 5 min read</small><h2><a href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/choosing-an-appraisal-umpire/">How an Appraisal Umpire Is Chosen, and Why It Matters</a></h2><p>The umpire decides the items the appraisers can’t settle. Here is how one is selected and what makes a good choice.</p></div></article><article class="gcard rv"><a class="gcard-ph" href="/kansas-appraisal-guides/matching-siding-shingles-after-hail/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/siding.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/siding-640.we